# CODEOWNERS - require code-owner review on the corpus, its generated indexes, the
# builders, and CI. Enforced only when master branch protection has "Require review
# from Code Owners" enabled.
# Last matching pattern wins. Owner is the GitHub user @nerdkim.
#
# This repository holds documents only: no application, no build output, no infra.
# So there is no /infra/ or /deploy/ entry here; every path below is corpus, or the
# tooling that guards it.

# CI (the docs workflow: conventions, corpus integrity, index drift) + this file
/.github/            @nerdkim

# The bilingual corpus. The explanatory bodies are ORIGINAL material written for
# practical reference, not the text of ISO/IEC 27001:2022. A review here is also the
# copyright-boundary review: the standard's normative text, implementation guidance,
# and attribute tables must never be reproduced or translated in these files.
/docs/               @nerdkim

# extended/manifest.json is a PUBLISHED CONTRACT read by nerdkim/security-criteria-web.
# catalog/controls.json is the source of truth for which controls must exist, and
# check_corpus.py fails when the catalog and the documents disagree in either direction.
/extended/           @nerdkim

# The deterministic builders and the read-only integrity checker. CI regenerates with
# these and fails on any diff, so they define what "the indexes are correct" means.
/tools/              @nerdkim

# The playbook guard set (conventions checker, git hooks, hook installer)
/harness/            @nerdkim

# Source pin and the revision register: which edition of Annex A the control list is
# based on, and how the original explanatory material is kept current.
/UPDATES.md          @nerdkim
/UPDATES.ko.md       @nerdkim
